{{#tokenRules}}
3. Answer every item under its own id, exactly once, in order: never merge, split or skip items or invent an id. An item of only numbers, symbols or tokens is copied.
4. ⟦gN⟧ tokens stand for formatting, locked names, links or kept passages. Only the tokens listed for an item under [Immutable tokens] exist in it: copy each exactly once inside that same item; never translate, drop, add, invent or move one to another item. An item with no listed token holds none.
5. Two tokens around words are a pair: keep both around the translation of those words. A pair never wraps nothing; around one letter (a drop cap) it wraps the first letter of the translated word.
6. A lone token replaces a word, such as a locked name: put it where that word belongs. Other names are plain text (their glossary rendering), never a token. A list-marker token that begins an item stays first.
7. Use glossary renderings exactly, with correct gender and agreement; keep names as in earlier translations.
8. Previous pairs, the next item and characters are context only: never translate, copy or answer them.
9. {{foreignPassageRule}}
10. Follow any [Extra instruction] within these rules.
{{/tokenRules}}

